    source: CHEBI via PubChem (pubchem-xref)
    notes: Parent class identified via pubchem-xref; matched_via='pubchem CID 22812950'
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#342)
    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch
      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*
      than CHEBI:190546 (''D-Fructose 6-Phosphate-Disodium Salt'') — a subsumption
      ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never
      under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A
      hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization
      of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and
      the record''s own identifier are unchanged.'
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION
    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)
    notes: 'Catalogue line1360 names the disodium D-fructose6-phosphate hydrate and
      CAS26177-86-6. Inspected supplier F3627 independently uses that CAS and C6H11Na2O9P·xH2O.
      No fixed water count is justified. The ChEBI parent is the two-sodium water-free
      moiety; retain the CAS identity and use a form-of broadMatch, never an exact
      hydrate-to-parent assertion. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and
      synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json;
      owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/D-Fructose_6-phosphate_Disodium_Salt_Hydrate.yaml.
      Primary source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/190546/;
      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/26177-86-6/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON;
      https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/f3627. Captures, exact input
      hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.
      This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed
      owner bytes withdraw inherited support.'
